    "message": {
     "content": "### The Verdict: **This is a top-of-market offer.**\n\nYour Google L6 offer is exceptional. A typical Google L6 PM total compensation package ranges between **$480,000 and $550,000** per year. Your offer significantly outperforms market medians and delivers a massive financial leap compared to your Meta IC6 compensation.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Side-by-Side Financial Comparison\n\nGoogle uses a **front-loaded vesting schedule** for initial grants: **33% (Year 1) / 33% (Year 2) / 22% (Year 3) / 12% (Year 4)**. \n\n| Component | Meta IC6 (Current) | Google L6 (Year 1) | Google L6 (Year 2) | Google L6 (Year 3) | Google L6 (Year 4) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $52,000 (20%) | $52,000 | $52,000 | $52,000 |\n| **Initial RSU Vest** | ~$250,000 *(~$200k next 12m)* | $442,200 *(33%)* | $442,200 *(33%)* | $294,800 *(22%)* | $160,800 *(12%)* |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | \u2014 | $200,000 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| **Annual Refreshes** | Stacking | \u2014 | Starts vesting | Overlapping | Overlapping |\n| **Total Compensation** | **~$526,000/yr** | **$954,200** | **$754,200 + Refreshes** | **$606,800 + Refreshes** | **$472,800 + Refreshes** |\n\n#### Key Takeaways:\n* **Year 1 Cash Flow:** You will make nearly **$1,000,000** in Year 1 (an 80%+ increase over your current Meta total comp).\n* **4-Year Total Baseline:** Without accounting for stock appreciation or annual refreshers, the 4-year total is **$2.79M**, or an average of **~$697,000/year** (a ~$171k/yr baseline increase).\n* **Refresher Mechanics:** While Google's initial grant drops in Years 3 and 4, annual refreshers (which Google typically grants annually with a multi-year vesting schedule) stack to help backfill that drop.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Component Benchmarking\n\n* **Base Salary ($260,000):** The posted range was $183,000\u2013$271,000. You are at the **96th percentile** of the band.\n* **Sign-On Bonus ($200,000):** Typical L6 sign-on bonuses range from $50,000 to $100,000. A $200,000 cash sign-on is at the extreme high end.\n* **Equity ($1.34M / 4 yrs):** Standard L6 initial grants range between $800k and $1.1M over 4 years. At $1.34M, Google has priced this near the top decile for an L6 PM.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Strategy: Accept, Negotiate, or Walk Away?\n\n* **Do not walk away** on compensation grounds.\n* **Should you negotiate?** **Yes, but with precision.** Because you are passive and happy at Meta, you have leverage. However, since Google is already close to the top of its compensation bands for L6, an aggressive counter-offer could trigger internal approval delays. A polite, anchored ask targeting **equity** is standard and will not risk the offer.\n\n#### Where is the remaining leverage?\n1. **Equity (Highest Probability):** Ask to bring the equity grant to **$1,450,000 \u2013 $1,500,000** over 4 years.\n2. **Base Salary (Low Impact):** You could ask for the top of the band (**$270,000**), but base bands have strict compensation committee caps.\n3. **Sign-on Bonus:** $200,000 is already near the ceiling; pushing this further is unlikely to yield results.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What to Ask For & How to Frame It\n\nAnchor your conversation on your strong standing at Meta, the comfort of your existing role, and bridging the gap to make the decision an immediate \"yes.\"\n\n#### Script / Email Framework:\n\n> *\"Thank you again for putting together this offer. I really enjoyed meeting the team, and I\u2019m excited about the scope and product direction we discussed.*\n> \n> *As mentioned, I wasn\u2019t actively looking to leave Meta and am in a strong position here with upcoming vesting cycles and momentum. Compensation is a key factor in making this transition. To close the gap and make this an immediate and easy decision for me to sign, is there flexibility to bring the equity grant to **$1.45M** (or top out the base salary at **$270k**)?*\n> \n> *If we can get to that number, I\u2019m ready to sign right away.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Key Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Terms:** Verify the clawback period (typically 12 months at Google) and payment schedule (payable in your first paycheck).\n2. **Meta Bonus Timing vs. Google Start Date:** If you have an upcoming Meta bonus payout date, set your start date at Google immediately after that payout so you do not leave earned cash on the table.\n3. **Vesting Cadence:** Confirm that the initial grant follows the 33/33/22/12 schedule and vests on a monthly/quarterly schedule.",
